Package: viewos-face-daemon
Source: viewos
Version: 0.1.0
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: ViewOS Project <help@jmultimate.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/Mitchell-Brooke/viewos
Depends:
 libopencv-core410,
 libopencv-imgproc410,
 libopencv-dnn410,
 libopencv-calib3d410,
 libopencv-videoio410,
 ${shlibs:Depends},
Recommends: viewos-kwin-effect
Description: Face tracking daemon for ViewOS head-tracked window perspective
 This daemon captures frames from a webcam, locates the viewer's face with a
 locally executed YuNet model, estimates head pose from the resulting facial
 landmarks, and publishes the pose over a local Unix socket.
 .
 The companion KWin effect, viewos-kwin-effect, reads that socket and rotates
 windows to face the viewer.
 .
 All processing happens on the local machine. The daemon contains no network
 functionality: it opens no sockets other than the Unix domain socket under
 /run/viewos, and writes nothing outside its configuration directory.
